title: the region
pid: c3f38641-3082-4cc2-9a3f-de869b5ae8d3
body: |2-
  What a subscription to A covers. Two candidates:
  - the author's: what A contains now, recursively. It drops what the author removed from A even where A' still holds it.
  - the follower's: what A' shows, recursively, with override substitution. It follows what one actually sees, but then must leave out one's own additions.
  Either way: hides prune the walk; one's own nodes stop it; a node one
  forked is passed through its overrider, whose subscription counts its
  first layer; a third author's nodes are a choice; and the walk needs
  a visited set.
